s2-2-p8 : Block
s2-2-p8 = prose (cons "The same construction pattern applies to a semantic judgment. For example, a big-step relation \(\mathsf{Eval}(e,v)\) can be an inductive family whose constructors are the evaluation rules; alternatively, when evaluation is a function, it can be defined as \(\llbracket e\rrbracket=v\). The two presentations may be related by an equivalence of their witness types, established by induction on derivations. A semantics is the defined structure and its equalities, not a second layer that has to be connected to mathematics afterward." nil)
